# Lab 7: Catch the Brute Force Attacker

## About This Lab

For this investigation, I examined network traffic to identify suspicious login activity associated with a possible brute-force attack.

The exercise focused on recognising repeated authentication attempts and identifying the source of suspicious activity.

## What I Worked On

- Examining captured network traffic.
- Investigating repeated login attempts.
- Identifying suspicious authentication patterns.
- Analysing IP addresses associated with the activity.
- Completing all 10 tasks in the lab.

## What I Learned

I learned how repeated authentication attempts can indicate a brute-force attack and how network traffic analysis can help identify suspicious login activity.

